            <ArticleTitle>Juvenile recurrent respiratory papillomatosis: A rare masquerade of asthma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>45-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Juvenile recurrent respiratory papillomatosis (JRRP) is a rare condition. The varied presentation of this condition predisposes to misdiagnosis and potential life-threatening airway obstruction. In this paper, we have reported a case of JRRP presenting as severe respiratory distress and consequently mistreated as asthmatic attack culminating in a near fatal acute airway obstruction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
